    metaDescription: "Complete guide to Australian government scholarships for international students in 2026 — Australia Awards, Endeavour, and university-specific programs with full application details.",
    excerpt: "Australia offers significant government scholarship funding for international students. Here's everything you need to know about Australian Awards and other programs in 2026.",
    content: `<h2>Australia's Commitment to International Scholarship Funding</h2><p>Australia invests significantly in international scholarships as part of its foreign policy and aid strategy. The flagship programs — particularly Australia Awards — represent some of the most comprehensive fully funded scholarship packages available globally.</p>
    <h2>Australia Awards Scholarships</h2><p>Australia Awards are the premier Australian government scholarship for international students from the Indo-Pacific, Africa, and the Middle East. They fund full degrees — bachelor's, master's, or PhD — at Australian universities. Benefits include: full tuition, return airfare, an establishment allowance of AUD $5,000, a fortnightly living stipend, Overseas Student Health Cover, pre-course English language training, and fieldwork support where relevant. Approximately 4,500 awards are made annually. Applications typically open in February and close in April for the following year's intake.</p>
    <h2>Research Training Program (RTP) Scholarships</h2><p>The Australian Government funds the Research Training Program, which provides fee offsets and living allowances for domestic and international higher degree research students. These are distributed by universities, so apply directly to universities with strong research profiles in your area.</p>
    <h2>University-Specific Scholarships</h2><p>Every major Australian university offers merit-based scholarships for international students. The University of Melbourne's Graduate Research Scholarships, UNSW's Scientia PhD Scholarship (offering premium stipend of AUD $50,000 + tuition), and ANU's Chancellor's International Scholarship are particularly prestigious.</p>
    <h2>Equity and Development Scholarships</h2><p>The Australia Awards Short Course awards and fellowship programs fund professionals and emerging leaders from priority countries for short-term capacity development activities, typically 2–4 weeks in Australia. These are different from degree scholarships but equally valuable for career development.</p>
    <h2>How to Apply for Australia Awards</h2><p>Applications go through the Australia Awards online portal (oasis.dfat.gov.au). You apply to your home country's managing partner (often a government ministry or DFAT office). The selection process involves written applications, referee reports, and in some countries, interviews conducted by the Australian Embassy.</p>`,
    author: "Lena Fischer",
    authorRole: "Australia Education Consultant",
    readTime: "10 min read",
