    excerpt: "Everything you need to know about obtaining an Australian Student Visa (Subclass 500) in 2026 — documents, GTE statement, financial proof, and health requirements.",
    content: `<h2>About the Australian Student Visa (Subclass 500)</h2><p>The Student Visa (Subclass 500) allows international students to study full-time at an Australian educational institution. It is valid for the duration of your enrolled course plus a short additional period. It is one of the most comprehensive student visa categories globally, allowing significant work rights alongside study.</p>
    <h2>Eligibility Requirements</h2><p>You must: be enrolled in a registered course with a CRICOS-registered provider; meet the Genuine Temporary Entrant (GTE) requirement; demonstrate financial capacity; meet English language requirements; provide health examination results if required; provide character documentation; and have valid health insurance (Overseas Student Health Cover – OSHC).</p>
    <h2>The Genuine Temporary Entrant (GTE) Requirement</h2><p>This is the most critical component. You must demonstrate that studying in Australia serves a genuine educational purpose and that you intend to stay temporarily. Evidence includes: your immigration history; your ties to your home country (family, employment, assets); your career plans at home after graduation; and how the course fits your career trajectory. A GTE statement of approximately 400–600 words is typically submitted as a supporting document.</p>
    <h2>Financial Requirements</h2><p>You must demonstrate: tuition fees for the first year of your course; living costs of AUD $29,710 per year for the primary visa holder; AUD $10,440 per year per accompanying adult family member; and AUD $4,449 per child per year. Evidence: bank statements, scholarship letters, loan approval letters.</p>
    <h2>English Language Requirements</h2><p>For university-level study: IELTS Academic 6.0+ overall (with no band below 5.0); TOEFL iBT 64+; PTE Academic 50+. Some universities and scholarship programs require higher scores (IELTS 6.5–7.0).</p>
    <h2>Overseas Student Health Cover (OSHC)</h2><p>OSHC is mandatory for the full duration of your student visa. It must be arranged before you apply for your visa. Providers include: Medibank, Bupa, Allianz Care Australia, AHM, and CBHS. Costs vary — annual premiums range from AUD $600–$850 for single students.</p>
    <h2>How to Apply</h2><p>Apply online through Australia's ImmiAccount portal (immi.homeaffairs.gov.au). Processing times vary: 75% of applications are processed within 22–42 days; 90% within 2–3 months. Apply at least 3 months before your course start date. Biometrics may be required at a visa application centre in your country.</p>`,
